    "media:imagetext": "A San Francisco Airport Commission Exhibition\nSan Francisco International Airport\nBuilding For Air Travel\nArchitecture and Design for Commercial Aviation\nAIRPORTS\nPictured at center: Skidmore, Owings \u0026 Merrill, Del Campo \u0026 Maru, Michael Walls \u0026 Associates, Joint Venture Architects. Model of the New International Terminal for San\nFrancisco International Airport, 1993-2000. Photographs clockwise from upper left: Eeero Saarinen, architect. Trans Woeld Airlines Terminal, John F. Kennedy Internationa\nAirport, New York, 1956-62, 1970. Ezra Stoller, photographer; Von Gerkan, Marg \u0026 Partners, architects Hamburg International Airport, 1986-94. Michael Wortmann.\nphotographer, courtesy of Von Gerkan, Marg \u0026 Partners, Murphy/Jahn Architects. Helmut Jahn of Murphy/Jahn Architect. Terminal 1 at O'Hare International Airport, 1988.\nHans Ege, photographer, courtesy of Murphy/Jahn Architects; Pier Luigi Nervi, architect. Hangar at the Air Force Base at Orvieto, Italy, 1945. From Moderne Bauformen (1939).\nOrganized by The Art Institute of Chicago\nMajor support for this exhibitice was provided by the National Endowmeat for the Humanities. Additional funding was provided by Lufthane German Airtisis. United Airlines and th\nBenefactors of Architecsure at The Art Institute of Chicago\nOn View Now\nIn the International Terminal\nNorth Connector Gallery\nLocated on the Upper\nLevel between Boarding\nArea D and Boarding\nArea F",
